WHY THE PATCH
-------------
`solve_dc_current` returns powertrain-sign current (P < 0 on discharge => I < 0),
while `dc_voltage = ocv - R0*I - v_rc1 - v_rc2` and both RC updates assume battery-sign
current (discharge positive). The two conventions meet with no conversion. Measured on
the unpatched source: 60 s at I = -100 A with stock R1, R2, TAU1, TAU2 gives
v_rc1 = -10,000 V, v_rc2 = -0,476 V, Udc = 790,5 V against OCV = 780 V — terminal
voltage above OCV while discharging.

The conversion is made once, immediately after the solver, so `dc_voltage`, both RC
updates and the KT2*I**2 heating term are untouched and become correct by construction.


THE SIX EDITS
-------------
(1) main.py:374 — inserted immediately after `dc_current = solve_dc_current(...)`

    +            # Battery perspective from here on: positive = discharge. See PLANT_ORIGIN.
    +            dc_current = -dc_current

(2) main.py:377,379 — the two saturation guards, comparisons flipped

    -            if q_act <= 0.0 and dc_current < 0.0:
    +            if q_act <= 0.0 and dc_current > 0.0:
                     dc_current = 0.0
    -            if q_act >= Q_MAX and dc_current > 0.0:
    +            if q_act >= Q_MAX and dc_current < 0.0:
                     dc_current = 0.0

(3) main.py:390 — coulomb counting

    -            q_act += dc_current * SAMPLE_TIME
    +            q_act -= dc_current * SAMPLE_TIME

(4) signals.json:143 — `dc_current_a` description

    -      "description": "DC current after temperature derating. Negative = discharge, positive = charge.",
    +      "description": "DC current after temperature derating. Positive = discharge, negative = charge (battery perspective).",

(5) main.py:455 — the inter-tick sleep, divided by the new TIME_SCALE parameter

    -            time.sleep(SAMPLE_TIME)
    +            time.sleep(SAMPLE_TIME / p["TIME_SCALE"])

    Only the wall-clock sleep is divided. The integration step stays SAMPLE_TIME at
    main.py:116 (both ALPHA), 390 (coulomb counting) and 414 (heat), so the published
    series is identical at any speed and the four trace sha256s are unaffected — the
    offline generator never sleeps at all: plant/loader.py:160 replaces main.time with
    a shim whose sleep discards its argument. `p` is the per-tick snapshot taken under
    state_lock at main.py:338, the same read the rest of the loop body uses.
    TIME_SCALE's lexicon min of 1.0 is what makes the divide safe; there is no guard.

(6) parameters.json — TIME_SCALE appended as the 19th descriptor

    +      "name": "TIME_SCALE",  "label": "Simulation Speed",  "datatype": "float",
    +      "unit": null,  "default": 1.0,  "min": 1.0,  "max": 50.0,  "tunable": true

    Reformatted here for width; the descriptor and its description are in the file.
    Tunable because it enters no state update, no filter coefficient and no integral,
    so a mid-run write breaks no continuity — the stated reason Q_MAX_AH and
    SAMPLE_TIME are fixed does not apply to it. max 50.0 is a throughput bound:
    ×50 is 500 msg/s on battery-data. model.version stays 1.1.0 because load_lexicon
    takes `model` wholesale from signals.json (lexicon.py:64), so bumping it here
    alone would leave the merged view and the [STARTUP] log reporting a stale number.


